<title>BELGIUM: Arbed falls into loss in 1996.</title>
<headline>Arbed falls into loss in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(in billion Luxembourg francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net loss (ex minorities)  1.207 vs   3.660 profit</p>
<p>    Cons net loss			 0.928 vs   6.615 profit</p>
<p>NOTE - Arbed is a Luxembourg-based steel group.  </p>
<p>    Turnover			    232.226 vs 257.105</p>
<p>    Gross operating profit	   19.477 vs  30.707</p>
<p>    Cash flow			    10.497 vs  22.681</p>
<p>    Own funds			    98.625 vs 100.797</p>
<p>	(group share)		    66.844 vs  67.720</p>
<p>    Parent company profit	     0.767 vs   1.369</p>
<p>NOTE: Arbed said in a statement it had substantially reduced net financial charges in 1996 of 6.7 billion francs, an exceptional loss of 0.7 billion and taxes of 840 million. It gave no comparative figures.</p>
<p>Arbed said after large investments net financial debt rose to 81.6 billion from 75.9 billion at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>It said the loss generated by long products had not been compensated for by positive results in the group's other sectors.</p>
<p>Production figures (in millions of tonnes):</p>
<p>    Iron ore, pellets and pellet feed  21.831  vs 21.840</p>
<p>    Crude steel				11.769  vs 11.501</p>
<p>    Rolled products			  10.907  vs 10.642</p>
<p>	includes flat products		6.490  vs  6.153</p>
<p>		   long products		3.974  vs  4.033</p>
<p>		   stainless steel	    0.443  vs  0.456</p>
<p>    Wire products			     0.831  vs  0.781</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
